# Constitution

Before translating an R package, read `ai-handbook/CONSTITUTION.md` and follow it. If the user says start, continue, or do it, and does not name a strategy, follow `ai-handbook/strategies/orchestrator.md`. Keep **25** translation sub-agents running; when one finishes, launch the next doable batch until the fleet is back at 25. Translation sub-agents pass the orchestrator model slug on Task `model`; do not use `inherit` for those launches. If the user names `ai-handbook/strategies/orchestrator.md`, follow it. Otherwise follow the one strategy they name under `ai-handbook/strategies/`, or the package field `strategy`. Follow the Experience section of `ai-handbook/CONSTITUTION.md`: open at most three of the filenames you name, and do not open the rest. Read `ai-handbook/NATIVE.md` when a function uses the R session, a project root, or the path of the running script. A sub-agent may add or edit one lesson in the file whose name matches the fact. The registry rules in `package-config` still apply.
